   "start": 64.9669,
   "end": 169.079,
   "text": "On the ground floor there are two shops, a hair studio at number 10 and a nail parlour business at number 12, each on a 10 -year lease at \u00a310 ,000 a year. Above the shops there are two HMOs, three rooms over number 10 and four rooms over number 12, averaging \u00a3680 a month per room, bills included. And to the rear, with its own access on Westcourt Street, there's a self -contained flat let at \u00a313 ,200 a year. In total, it's 3 ,829 square feet across all five units. Now the numbers. The passing rent is \u00a390 ,320 a year, which is a 9 % gross yield at the asking price. The landlord pays the bills on the HMO rooms, which come to \u00a3995 a month. Take those off and the income is \u00a378 ,380 or 7 .8 % net yield. Residential makes up 78 % of the income and the shop makes up 22%. Because it's a mixed -use building, stamp duty is charged at non -residential rates. At the asking price, that's \u00a339 ,500. With a 30 % deposit and interest -only finance at 6%, the income after interest is $36 ,380 a year, which is a 10 .7 % return on cash you put in. Those figures are illustrative and set out in the investment summary. The shop leases have tenant",
